hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"84","[AI-translation] Tareef sirf Allah ke liye hai; salat wa salam us par jis ke baad koi nabi nahin [Muhammad]. [Istikhara jaisi duaon ke shuru mein kahe]"
"85","[AI-translation] Shaitane-rajeem se Allah ki panah chahta hun. Allah; us ke siwa koi mabud nahin; woh zinda hai, qayam rakhne wala hai; use oongh-neend nahin pakadti. Aasmanon-zameen mein jo hai usi ka hai. Us ki ijazat ke baghair us ke pas kaun sifarish karega? Un ke aage-peeche jo hai woh janta hai; us ke ilm mein se kuch nahin gherte—woh jo chahe us ke siwa. Us ki kursi aasmanon-zameen ko ghere hai; un ki hifazat use thakati nahin; woh buland, Azeem hai. [surah Al-Baqarah:255 – Aayatul-Kursi; subah-sham padhe]"
"86","[AI-translation] Rahman wa Raheem Allah ke naam se. Kaho: Woh Allah ek hai. Allah beniyaz hai. Na us ne jana aur na woh jana gaya. Aur us ka koi hamsar nahin. [surah Al-Ikhlas:1-4] Rahman wa Raheem Allah ke naam se. Kaho: makhluq ke shar se subah ke Rab ki panah chahta hun; andhera chha jaane par raat ke shar se; girhon mein phunkne waliyon ke shar se; hasad kare to hasid ke shar se. [surah Al-Falaq:1-5] Rahman wa Raheem Allah ke naam se. Kaho: logon ke Rab, logon ke Badshah, logon ke mabud ki panah chahta hun; peeche hatne wale waswasa dalne wale ke shar se; jo logon ke seenon mein waswasa dalta hai; jinnon aur insanon [mein se]. [surah An-Naas:1-6] [Subah-sham teen-teen bar padhe]"
"87","[AI-translation] Hum ne subah ki, badshahat bhi Allah ke liye subah hui; tareef Allah ke liye hai. Allah ke siwa koi mabud nahin; woh akela hai, beshareek. Badshahat usi ki hai, tareef usi ki hai; woh har cheez par qadir hai. Ae mere Rab! Is din ki bhalai aur baad ki bhalai Tujhse mangta hun; is din ke shar aur baad ke shar se teri panah chahta hun. Ae mere Rab! Susti aur buri budhape se teri panah chahta hun. Ae mere Rab! Aag ke azab aur qabr ke azab se teri panah chahta hun. [Subah ka zikr; sham ko sham ke andaz mein]"
"88","[AI-translation] Ae Allah! Tere sath hum ne subah ki, tere sath sham ki, tere sath jeete hain, tere sath marte hain; teri hi taraf lautna hai. [Subah ka zikr]"
